  m_Name: game-design-document
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GameTerms.Runtime::GameTerms.GlossaryTermAsset
  data:
    Id: game-design-document
    Term: Game Design Document
    Abbreviation: gdd
    Category: 9
    Difficulty: 0
    ShortDefinition: A living reference that captures vision, systems, constraints,
      and content goals.
    SimpleExplanation: The shared write-up of what the game is and how its systems
      should work.
    WhyItMatters: A clear GDD reduces misalignment across design, art, engineering,
      and production.
    Example: Pillars, core loop, camera rules, and progression charts live in one
      editable doc.
    CommonMistake: Writing a huge unread GDD once, then never updating it as the
      game changes.
    PracticePrompt: Create a two-page GDD covering pillars, core loop, and out-of-scope
      list.
    GameUses:
    - Kickoffs
    - Vendor handoff
    - Vertical slice planning
    RelatedTermIds:
    - mvp
    - vertical-slice
    - milestone
    Tags:
    - documentation
    - design
    - production
    Synonyms:
    - GDD
    CodeExample: 
    HasDiagram: 0
    DiagramType: 0
    AddedAtUnix: 1716076800
